From dd2dfd283562b40b112fd0327c67ecb583c9eb43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Basin Battle <basin@battle>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:31:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Ground markers for an aimed ability and blows coming down;
 creature wind-ups that coil and snap; the right button the add-on's

SetAimMarker("circle", range, radius) lays a terrain-projected circle where the reticle's line
lands within range (as the Elwynn Survival server traces it: from the eye and the shoulder, along
the view's facing and elevation, pulled back to the range and dropped to the ground), and
GetAimPoint() reads it back. SetGroundMarker(key, x, y, z, radius, seconds[, hostile]) and
ClearGroundMarker([key]) lay timed circles (red for what's coming at us). Both use the
ground-targeting reticle's projector and textures. HasActionCombat() is 5.

A creature's wind-up asked to run well past its clip's own pace no longer plays as one slow
motion: the clip goes at its own speed into the coil, holds there, and snaps onto its impact at
1.8 times its speed, landing when the server says.

Under the action mouse the right button is the add-on's binding (the guard): its release no
longer ends a script's MouselookStart (the steering mouse), and it arms no right-click interact.
